  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "The diamond – back and deep",
  "description": "Players stand in four to six lines round a diamond: one line at each end (A and D) and lines along both sides (B and C on one side). A passes out to B, who has moved wide to give width. B plays it back to A, who straight away plays the ball in behind to C. C has started the run in good time and passes on to D. Rotate one step forward: A to B, B to C, C to D.\n\nAt the same time D starts the same pattern the other way along the far side. Switch sides after a few minutes so the pattern runs the other way. Use a big area (about 45 × 40 metres) for long passes, or about 20 × 15 metres with four lines for quick, short touches. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up before the ball arrives, so you see the runner in behind."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The runner goes in good time – before the team-mate gets the ball and looks up."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The player giving width stays wide and open to the pitch."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "The pass back should be straight and easy to play on first time."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
